<title>FINLAND: NESTE'S BOREALIS SELLS EVA OPERATION.</title>
<headline>NESTE'S BOREALIS SELLS EVA OPERATION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petrochemicals group Borealis -- jointly owned by Finland's Neste and Norwegian Statoil -- said on Wednesday it wes selling its ethylene vinyl acetate (EVA) operation to Exxon Chemical Europe, part of Exxon .</p>
<p>A Borealis spokeswoman said the deal was a similar disposal of non-core units to the company's sale earlier this month of its car interior parts maker Borealis Industrier.</p>
<p>She declined to specify any financial details.</p>
<p>Exxon was buying Borealis' clients, technical know-how, inventories and deliveries due, but fixed assets and personnel were excluded from the deal, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
